wincan
======

wincan is a Windows GUI and a Linux server to view your stock and crypto charts in real time, and see your
win/loss as it happens.  The chart is a small window that stays on top of your desktop, or full screen on f.  It is keyboard
driven, built for speed, responsiveness and good feel, and uses the mouse tastefully so it stays fast.

  wincan.exe   the window: 300x175 pixels, no frame, always on top, candles with indicators, the last price, your
               position's profit and loss, a liquidation heat strip, full screen on f; one file, nothing but Windows.
  candled      the candle supply, for Linux (Debian, Ubuntu, WSL2, Fedora and relatives, Alpine): serves candles as JSON
               over TLS to the clients whose key it has been told, by the SHA-256 fingerprint of their own certificate
               (as an IRC bouncer does with certfp).  Its settings are in candled.conf.

Install:      see INSTALL.  In short:   ./configure && make && make check && make install
              sudo sh linux/install-candled.sh                 the server: user, key, service
              powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File windows/install.ps1 -Server https://HOST:8766   the window
Use:          man wincan, man candled, man candled.conf, man candle-protocol, man wincan(5) for wincan.ini
Hack on it:   see HACKING.  The configuration parser is generated by hbnf (https://github.com/moebiusV/hbnf) from
              grammars/candled.hbnf and committed; building needs no hbnf.
Licence:      GNU GPL, version 3 or later (COPYING).  Report bugs at https://github.com/moebiusV/wincan/issues

README.md is the same story with pictures.  NEWS says what changed; ChangeLog how; AUTHORS and THANKS who.
